To perform text analysis using natural language processing and generate a comparison report between the main theme in Romeo and Juliet and other works of Shakespeare, you can use a PHP library like Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) or Stanford CoreNLP. Here's an example code snippet using NLTK:
```php
// Import NLTK library
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
use \NlpTools\Tokenizers\WhitespaceTokenizer;
use \NlpTools\Stemmers\PorterStemmer;
use \NlpTools\Similarity\CosineSimilarity;
// Load the text of Romeo and Juliet and other works of Shakespeare
$romeo_and_juliet = file_get_contents("http://shakespeare.mit.edu/romeo_juliet/full.html");
$shakespeare = file_get_contents("http://shakespeare.mit.edu/");
// Remove HTML tags and lowercase the text
$romeo_and_juliet_text = strtolower(strip_tags($romeo_and_juliet));
$shakespeare_text = strtolower(strip_tags($shakespeare));
// Tokenize the text into words
