What Java code can be used to check if a string is a palindrome?
Please provide a Java code snippet in the following format:
public class PalindromeChecker {
  public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
    // your code here
  }
}
The method should return true if the input string is a palindrome (i.e. reads the same forwards and backwards), and false otherwise.
For example, calling isPalindrome("racecar") should return true, while calling isPalindrome("hello") should return false.

output:
Here's a Java code snippet that checks if a string is a palindrome:
```
public class PalindromeChecker {
  public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
    // Remove all non-letter characters and convert to lowercase
    String cleanStr = str.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z]", "").toLowerCase();

    // Check if the string is empty or has only one character
    if (cleanStr.length() <= 1) {
      return true;
    }

    // Compare the first and last characters of the string
    if (cleanStr.charAt(0) != cleanStr.charAt(cleanStr.length() - 1)) {
      return false;
    }

    // Recursively check the substring without the first and last characters
    return isPalindrome(cleanStr.substring(1, cleanStr.length() - 1));
  }
}
```
The code first removes all non-letter characters and converts the string to lowercase. It then checks if the string is empty or has only one character, in which case it is a palindrome by definition. If not, it compares the first and last characters of the string. If they are not equal, the string is not a palindrome. If they are equal, it recursively checks the substring without the first and last characters until the string is empty or has only one character. If all comparisons are equal, the string is a palindrome.

