There are several pre-processing techniques that can be applied to prevent overfitting when building a machine learning model. Some of these techniques include:
1. Data augmentation: This involves creating new training data by applying transformations such as rotation, scaling, and flipping to the original images. This increases the size of the training dataset and reduces overfitting.
2. Dropout: This technique involves randomly dropping out some neurons during training to prevent over-reliance on specific features and reduce overfitting.
3. Batch normalization: This involves normalizing the input data to each layer to reduce the internal covariate shift and improve the stability of the model during training.
Here's an example of how to apply data augmentation using the Keras library in C#:
```csharp
