2. Create a bag of words: Create a dictionary of all the words in the text and their frequency of occurrence.
3. Create feature vectors: Create feature vectors for the input text and the target and non-target words. A feature vector is a numerical representation of the text that the machine learning model can process. In this case, you can use the bag of words as the feature vector.
4. Train the model: Train the model using the feature vectors and the labels (target and non-target).
5. Evaluate the model: Evaluate the model's accuracy and precision using a test dataset.
